[21:12:22.981] << {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cd9RUJyVfuPWicS7TBdmx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"MaxVibes is an IntelliJ platform plugin (Kotlin, hexagonal/ports-and-adapters architecture) that turns the IDE into an AI coding assistant with deep PSI (code structure) integration, rather than a thin chat wrapper around an LLM.\n\n**Core idea:** the plugin gives an LLM (OpenAI/Anthropic via LangChain4j, or a headless Claude Code CLI process) structured, semantic access to your codebase — via PSI, not raw file text — so the model can request precise \"views\" of code (signatures, single functions, call hierarchies, usages) and apply changes as structural PSI operations (replace/create/delete a specific function, class, import) instead of freeform text diffs.\n\n**Module layout** (`maxvibes-domain`, `-application`, `-adapter-psi`, `-adapter-psi-python`, `-adapter-llm`, `-plugin`, `-shared`) follows clean/hexagonal architecture: domain model → application ports/services → adapters (PSI for Kotlin and Python, LLM providers, clipboard/process I/O) → the actual IntelliJ plugin module wiring it into the IDE UI.\n\n**Key features visible in the tree:**\n- A chat panel (`ChatPanel`, `ConversationPanel`, session tree/history) inside an IDE tool window.\n- Two interaction modes: direct LLM API calls, and a \"Claude Code\" mode that drives the `claude` CLI as a subprocess with a structured JSON protocol (`ClaudeCodeInteractionService`, stream-json parsing).\n- A **clipboard protocol** (`ClipboardProtocol`, `JsonInteractionProtocolCodec`) — an alternate copy/paste-based interaction channel, seemingly for using this with web-based Claude/ChatGPT UIs.\n- Code granularity system (`CodeGranularity`, `CodeElement`, `ElementPath`) letting the model ask for `SIGNATURES`, `OUTLINE`, `ELEMENT`, `USAGES`, `CALLERS`, etc. instead of whole files.\n- A **Planner** feature (currently in progress per `docs/features/Planner/` and the new `TaskPlan.kt` domain model) — a checklist/plan panel pinned above chat that the LLM updates as it works through multi-step tasks.\n- Editor actions, skills (`SKILL.md` files like `explain-element`, `find-smells`, `write-kdoc`), and Python support alongside Kotlin.\n\n**Development style:** the `docs/features/*` and `docs/refactors/*` directories show heavy use of step-by-step planning docs (PLAN.md + STEP_N_*.md per feature) — this project is itself built using an incremental, documented, AI-assisted workflow, which is fitting since the tool's purpose is to enable exactly that kind of workflow for its users.\n\nIn short: **it's a meta tool** — an IDE plugin, built with AI assistance, whose entire purpose is to make AI coding assistance more structurally aware and reliable by grounding it in PSI rather than raw text."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25028,"cache_read_input_tokens":14849,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25028},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75a63246-cd0f-4742-a144-6e8c2a5883a5","uuid":"8bbb2275-692a-475e-b360-f2d9e0879550","timestamp":"2026-07-18T11:12:22.973Z","request_id":"req_011Cd9RUHYB3V5MsEet4Xt5R"}
